.TH "PUT-BUCKET-NOTIFICATION-CONFIGURATION"  "" "" ""
.SH NAME
put-bucket-notification-configuration \- 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This operation is not supported for directory buckets.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Enables notifications of specified events for a bucket. For more information about event notifications, see \fI\%Configuring Event Notifications\fP .
.sp
Using this API, you can replace an existing notification configuration. The configuration is an XML file that defines the event types that you want Amazon S3 to publish and the destination where you want Amazon S3 to publish an event notification when it detects an event of the specified type.
.sp
By default, your bucket has no event notifications configured. That is, the notification configuration will be an empty \fBNotificationConfiguration\fP .
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fB<NotificationConfiguration>\fP
.sp
\fB</NotificationConfiguration>\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This action replaces the existing notification configuration with the configuration you include in the request body.
.sp
After Amazon S3 receives this request, it first verifies that any Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) or Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) destination exists, and that the bucket owner has permission to publish to it by sending a test notification. In the case of Lambda destinations, Amazon S3 verifies that the Lambda function permissions grant Amazon S3 permission to invoke the function from the Amazon S3 bucket. For more information, see \fI\%Configuring Notifications for Amazon S3 Events\fP .
.sp
You can disable notifications by adding the empty NotificationConfiguration element.
.sp
For more information about the number of event notification configurations that you can create per bucket, see \fI\%Amazon S3 service quotas\fP in \fIAmazon Web Services General Reference\fP .
.sp
By default, only the bucket owner can configure notifications on a bucket. However, bucket owners can use a bucket policy to grant permission to other users to set this configuration with the required \fBs3:PutBucketNotification\fP permission.
.sp
\fBNOTE:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The PUT notification is an atomic operation. For example, suppose your notification configuration includes SNS topic, SQS queue, and Lambda function configurations. When you send a PUT request with this configuration, Amazon S3 sends test messages to your SNS topic. If the message fails, the entire PUT action will fail, and Amazon S3 will not add the configuration to your bucket.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the configuration in the request body includes only one \fBTopicConfiguration\fP specifying only the \fBs3:ReducedRedundancyLostObject\fP event type, the response will also include the \fBx\-amz\-sns\-test\-message\-id\fP header containing the message ID of the test notification sent to the topic.
.sp
The following action is related to \fBPutBucketNotificationConfiguration\fP :
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\%GetBucketNotificationConfiguration\fP
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also: AWS API Documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.nf
.ft C
  put\-bucket\-notification\-configuration
\-\-bucket <value>
\-\-notification\-configuration <value>
[\-\-expected\-bucket\-owner <value>]
[\-\-skip\-destination\-validation | \-\-no\-skip\-destination\-validation]
[\-\-cli\-input\-json | \-\-cli\-input\-yaml]
[\-\-generate\-cli\-skeleton <value>]
[\-\-debug]
[\-\-endpoint\-url <value>]
[\-\-no\-verify\-ssl]
[\-\-no\-paginate]
[\-\-output <value>]
[\-\-query <value>]
[\-\-profile <value>]
[\-\-region <value>]
[\-\-version <value>]
[\-\-color <value>]
[\-\-no\-sign\-request]
[\-\-ca\-bundle <value>]
[\-\-cli\-read\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-connect\-timeout <value>]
[\-\-cli\-binary\-format <value>]
[\-\-no\-cli\-pager]
[\-\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
[\-\-no\-cli\-auto\-prompt]
.ft P
.fi
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
\fB\-\-bucket\fP (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The name of the bucket.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-notification\-configuration\fP (structure) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A container for specifying the notification configuration of the bucket. If this element is empty, notifications are turned off for the bucket.
.sp
TopicConfigurations \-> (list)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The topic to which notifications are sent and the events for which notifications are generated.
.sp
(structure)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
A container for specifying the configuration for publication of messages to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when Amazon S3 detects specified events.
.sp
Id \-> (string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
An optional unique identifier for configurations in a notification configuration. If you don\(aqt provide one, Amazon S3 will assign an ID.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
TopicArn \-> (string) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Amazon SNS topic to which Amazon S3 publishes a message when it detects events of the specified type.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Events \-> (list) [required]
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The Amazon S3 bucket event about which to send notifications. For more information, see \fI\%Supported Event Types\fP in the \fIAmazon S3 User Guide\fP .
.sp
(string)
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
The bucket event for which to send notifications.
.sp
